Build a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) Chatbot that answers user queries based on uploaded or pre-provided documents by leveraging NLP preprocessing, semantic chunking, embeddings, and vector similarity search.

🪄 Detailed Description

You are tasked with creating a RAG Chatbot that uses retrieval + generation techniques to deliver context-aware and factually grounded responses from custom documents.

Step-by-Step Process

Document Ingestion & Cleaning

Accept user documents (PDF, text, CSV, or HTML).

Perform preprocessing using NLP techniques such as:

Text normalization (lowercasing, punctuation removal)

Stopword removal

Lemmatization or stemming

Removing unwanted symbols, tables, or metadata noise

✅ Goal: Obtain clean and structured text ready for chunking.

Semantic Chunking

Split the cleaned text into meaningful chunks using semantic segmentation, not just by length.

Each chunk should preserve logical or contextual meaning (e.g., paragraph or section level).

Add metadata (e.g., document title, section heading, source filename).

✅ Goal: Maintain semantic integrity and context for each chunk.

Embedding Generation

Use embedding models (like OpenAI embeddings, SentenceTransformers, or Hugging Face models) to convert each chunk into vector embeddings.

Store the following for each chunk:

chunk_id

text_chunk

metadata

vector_embedding

✅ Goal: Represent textual meaning numerically for similarity-based retrieval.

Vector Storage (ChromaDB Integration)

Store all embeddings inside ChromaDB, a local or cloud-based vector database.

Ensure metadata is stored for filtering or contextual grouping.

✅ Goal: Enable fast and efficient similarity search for relevant chunks.

Query Processing & Retrieval

When a user sends a query, generate its embedding using the same embedding model.

Perform similarity search in ChromaDB to retrieve the top relevant chunks.

Use metadata filters if needed (e.g., document type or topic).

✅ Goal: Retrieve the most contextually relevant chunks.

Re-ranking & Context Enhancement

Apply Cross-Encoder re-ranking (optional but recommended) to refine retrieved chunks.

Select top-ranked chunks to form the context window.

Combine these chunks with the user’s query into a prompt template for the LLM.

✅ Goal: Improve retrieval precision before generating response.

Response Generation

Pass the context + user query into an LLM (e.g., GPT, Llama, or Mistral).

The model generates a natural-language response grounded in the retrieved data.

Optionally integrate memory and tools to make the chatbot agentic (e.g., persistent memory, calculator, web search).

✅ Goal: Produce accurate, context-rich, and explainable responses.

⚙️ Technologies & Tools

Language: Python

Libraries:

langchain or llama-index (for orchestration)

nltk, spacy, transformers (for NLP processing)

sentence-transformers (for embeddings)

chromadb (for vector storage)

LLMs: OpenAI, Anthropic Claude, or local Llama models

Optional Enhancements:

Add tool use (e.g., code interpreter, calculator)

Integrate memory for multi-turn conversation persistence
